:: Flirt Duty [event mom_quest] {"position":"4275,1075","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "Flirt Duty" (mom_flirtDuty), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 5.3. A comedy. In the morning at my desk I give her a new job: make the
   staff feel good about their work. She says she hasn't flirted since college, so I coach her, with myself as the practice
   target. Three rules, which I make her say back to me twice, like a phone number (her first round, Task Mom Flirt Duty 0,
   quotes them): look them in the eye, a hand on the arm for only a second, laugh at their jokes, especially the bad ones.
   Every time she tries to flirt, a mother comes out. Once, at the end, she gets it right, and the small proud smile shows
   for the first time. The quest's set activates task_mom_flirt_duty. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[14].img>><</silent>>
$mom.callName comes to my desk with her tablet and her morning face, the cheerful one with the to-do list behind it. She's got the client calendar open before she's even stopped walking.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Good morning, sweetie. So, today, the $diner.name invoice went out, $boss.callName wants Thursday instead of Wednesday, and somebody keeps putting fish in the office microwave and I have my suspicions." },
{ who: $player, text: "Got a minute? Sit down, it's nothing bad." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Is it the fish? Because I haven't said anything to anybody yet, I want to be sure first." },
{ who: $player, text: "It's not the fish. Although now I really want to know who it is." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She sits on the edge of the chair next to my desk with the tablet on her knees, ready to write down whatever's wrong.

<<linkreplace "Give her the new job">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "The team's working really hard, and the new project is going to be a lot harder, so I need them happy. Not only paid, actually happy, the kind where they come in early and stay late and don't even mind." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, I can do that! I'll bring in muffins, the lemon ones, everybody likes those. Well, except $brian.name, he doesn't like anything with a texture, but I'll find something for him." },
{ who: $player, text: "I was thinking of something besides muffins." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Cookies?" },
{ who: $player, text: "You. I want you to do a round through the office every day and talk to them, and make each one of them feel like the most interesting guy in the room for a few minutes." },
{ who: $mom, text: "But I do talk to them, honey, I talk to them all the time." },
{ who: $player, text: "You fuss over them. You sew their buttons back on and confiscate their noodles. I want you to flirt with them a little." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She looks at me as if I've asked her to do their taxes in Latin.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Flirt? With the boys?" },
{ who: $player, text: "A little. Nothing crazy, a smile and some attention." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Sweetheart, I haven't flirted since college, and I'm not sure I did it then either. I think I mostly stood around in kitchens until your $dad.relation found me." },
{ who: $mom, text: "And they're boys! Well, they're grown men, I know that, but they're... I mean, I'm old enough to be..." },
{ who: $player, text: "You're old enough to be really good at it, is what you are." },
{ text: "That one gets through. I can see it land, and I can see her decide to pretend it didn't." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Coach her">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "It's not complicated, I promise. There are really only three things, and if you remember those you'll be fine." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Should I write them down? Actually, no, I'm not typing the word 'flirt' into the company tablet, honey, it syncs with everything." },
{ who: $player, text: "The first one is eye contact. When you talk to them, look at them, not at their screen or their coffee or whatever's on their shirt." },
{ who: $mom, text: "There's always something on $ethan.name's shirt." },
{ who: $player, text: "Ignore it. Second, a hand on the arm, but only for a second, and then you take it back. If you leave it there it turns into comforting them, and you're not there to comfort anybody." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Hand on the arm, one second. Okay. And the third?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Laugh at their jokes. Especially the ones that aren't funny." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Even $ethan.name's?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Especially his. He'll know if you fake it, though, so you'll have to find something in there that's actually funny." },
{ who: $mom, text: "That's going to take a lot out of me, honey." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Make her practice">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Try it on me. Pretend I'm $darius.name. I'm at my desk, I'm very busy, and I'm extremely handsome." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, this is ridiculous." },
{ who: $player, text: "Come on, humor me. Walk over like you just happen to be passing by." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She stands up, smooths her skirt, walks three steps away from my desk, turns around and walks back. She stops beside me, looks me firmly in the eye, and puts her hand on my arm.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Hello, $darius.name. You look tired. Are you sleeping enough? You need to eat more than that salad." },
{ who: $player, text: "Okay, hang on, stop there." },
{ who: $mom, text: "What? I looked him in the eye!" },
{ who: $player, text: "You did, and then you asked him if he's sleeping enough." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Well, he doesn't look like he is!" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Again">>
The second try, she leans on my desk, which is better, and tells me that's a very nice tie, which is good, and then asks if I want her to iron it, which isn't.

The third try she gets through the eye contact and the hand on the arm and then forgets to take the hand back. It just stays there, patting me, the way she pats my arm at the dinner table when I've told her about my day.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "$mom.callName. You're patting me." },
{ who: $mom, text: "I know! I can feel it, and I can't make it stop!" },
{ text: "She snatches the hand back and holds it against her chest as if it bit her, and then she starts laughing, helplessly, with her other hand over her mouth, and I laugh too, because it's impossible not to." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Every time I open my mouth a $mom.relation comes out, honey, and I don't know how to turn it off, it's been switched on for twenty years." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "One more time">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "One more try. And this time, don't think about $darius.name at all. Think about how you'd want somebody to look at you, if somebody finally did." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

That stops her laughing. She stands there for a moment, and something in her face changes, gets quieter, and she walks the three steps away again and turns.

This time she takes her time coming back. She doesn't lean on the desk. She stops a little closer than she needs to and looks at me, not firmly this time, just looks, as if she has all the time in the world to decide what to say. Her fingers rest on my forearm, light as anything, and slide off again.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "I read your whole report last night, you know. You're much funnier on paper than you let anybody see." },
{ text: "And then she smiles, a slow, private kind of smile I have genuinely never seen on her face before, and walks off toward the copier without waiting for an answer." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She gets four steps before she turns around, completely pink.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, God. Was that too much? It felt like... I honestly don't know what that felt like." },
{ who: $player, text: "If I were $darius.name, I'd be staring at the copier right now trying to work out what just happened to me." },
{ who: $mom, text: "You're just saying that." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm not. Do that every day, with all three of them, and I'll be very happy with you." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

There it is: a small smile at the corner of her mouth that she presses flat as soon as she feels it. It comes right back. She presses it flat again.

<<linkreplace "Send her off">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Before you go, tell me the three things again. Humor me." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Look them in the eye, a hand on the arm for one second, and laugh at the bad jokes." },
{ who: $player, text: "Once more, because I know you, and by lunch it's going to be 'look them in the eye and ask if they've eaten.'" },
{ who: $mom, text: "Eye contact, hand on the arm, one second, I know, honey, and laugh at the bad jokes. I've got it. I'm not senile yet." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm putting your first round in the schedule, then. And I'll be watching." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, God, please don't watch, I'll be so much worse if I know you're watching." },
{ who: $player, text: "Sorry. I wouldn't miss it for anything." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She takes her tablet and goes back to her desk, and sits there for a while straightening things, and looks over at $ethan.name, and then at $darius.name, and then at $brian.name, the way a swimmer looks at cold water.

Then she opens her compact and checks her lipstick, which I have never seen her do at the office.

<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomRelation" 1>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 1>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomExhibition" 2>>
<<ProfileLog $mom "Flirt Duty" "I gave her a new job: one round a day through the office, making the staff feel like the most interesting men in the room. She said she hasn't flirted since college, so I made her practice on me until a $mom.relation stopped coming out. The last try was good. She was proud of it, and tried hard not to show it.">>
<<NextQuest $mom>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
